WEBVTT

00:00:11.444 --> 00:00:12.809
Look.

00:00:15.548 --> 00:00:18.108
And you said they were
incompatible.

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:22.177
You have confirmed
the genetic structure?

00:00:22.222 --> 00:00:25.214
An entirely new species.

00:00:25.258 --> 00:00:27.692
I'm going to name it after you.

00:00:27.727 --> 00:00:29.922
The Tuvok orchid.

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:34.490
That is an honor you should
reserve for yourself, Mr. Suder.

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:37.002
You gave this species life.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:38.594
And you gave me life.

00:00:38.638 --> 00:00:40.868
All of this is because of you.

00:00:43.643 --> 00:00:45.634
Because of the meld.

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:50.138
The meld may have introduced you
to my interest in floriculture,

00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:53.311
but you have embraced it
entirely on your own.

00:00:53.353 --> 00:00:56.811
And discovered a unique
talent within yourself

00:00:56.856 --> 00:00:58.016
in the process.

00:00:58.058 --> 00:01:01.687
I used to think
the only talent I had

00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:04.720
was a talent for killing.

00:01:04.764 --> 00:01:08.996
Please... it's my way
of saying thank you.

00:01:11.004 --> 00:01:12.596
Very well.

00:01:12.639 --> 00:01:14.334
I accept.

00:01:19.012 --> 00:01:22.948
Tuvok, I want to do
something for the ship.

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:25.815
I'm not asking you
to let me out of confinement.

00:01:25.852 --> 00:01:27.114
I accept my punishment.

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:29.621
But if I could just...

00:01:29.656 --> 00:01:32.352
just contribute somehow.

00:01:32.392 --> 00:01:34.860
What contribution do you
feel you could make

00:01:34.894 --> 00:01:36.327
from your quarters?

00:01:36.362 --> 00:01:40.765
I was... I was thinking
I might adapt

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:43.234
some of the genetic
engineering techniques

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:45.100
I've developed for the orchids

00:01:45.138 --> 00:01:48.198
to make the airponic vegetable
garden more productive.

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:51.271
Your attitude is admirable.

00:01:51.311 --> 00:01:54.576
I will discuss it
with the Captain.

00:01:54.614 --> 00:01:57.014
Do you think she'll agree?

00:01:58.017 --> 00:01:59.814
We'll see.

00:01:59.853 --> 00:02:01.377
Now, shall we begin?

00:02:05.425 --> 00:02:07.620
Notice your mind working.

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:10.424
How it plans for the future,

00:02:10.463 --> 00:02:12.693
visits the past.

00:02:12.732 --> 00:02:14.529
Notice those thoughts

00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:16.694
and set them aside.

00:02:16.736 --> 00:02:19.830
Turn your attention
to the white light

00:02:19.873 --> 00:02:22.307
that is your breath.

00:02:22.342 --> 00:02:25.140
Captain, we're being hailed
on a subspace frequency.

00:02:25.178 --> 00:02:26.907
Are there ships in the vicinity?

00:02:26.946 --> 00:02:29.141
Negative.
Tracking the source.

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:32.748
Seems likes it's coming
from an unmanned buoy.

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:36.243
Coordinates 140 mark 317.

00:02:36.289 --> 00:02:37.984
It looks like a Kazon signal,
Captain.

00:02:38.057 --> 00:02:40.287
Take us out of warp.

00:02:40.326 --> 00:02:41.884
Open a channel.

00:02:43.129 --> 00:02:46.360
Chakotay, they're going
to take your son.

00:02:46.399 --> 00:02:48.162
When Culluh saw the baby...

00:02:48.201 --> 00:02:49.793
I hear them coming.

00:02:49.836 --> 00:02:50.928
I don't have much time.

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:52.631
When he saw
the baby wasn't his...

00:02:52.672 --> 00:02:56.335
Please, Chakotay, help us...
not for me, for your son.

00:02:56.376 --> 00:02:58.276
I told you to stay out of here.

00:02:58.311 --> 00:02:59.869
No, please don't.

00:02:59.913 --> 00:03:01.676
Don't take him!

00:03:01.714 --> 00:03:04.706
I beg... No! Please, no.

00:03:04.751 --> 00:03:05.809
No!

00:05:00.098 --> 00:05:01.998
This is not my responsibility.

00:05:02.033 --> 00:05:03.523
She has no right to expect me...

00:05:03.568 --> 00:05:05.365
She knows you, Chakotay.

00:05:05.403 --> 00:05:08.930
She knew how you'd react
when you saw your son in danger.

00:05:08.973 --> 00:05:10.838
I have a duty to this crew.

00:05:10.875 --> 00:05:13.867
I can't just leave
and go looking for the child.

00:05:13.912 --> 00:05:15.436
And I'd never consider
letting you go

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:17.380
into a Kazon-Nistrim
stronghold by yourself.

00:05:17.415 --> 00:05:19.975
If we do this,
we do it together.

00:05:21.252 --> 00:05:23.652
That's something else
Seska would know, too.

00:05:23.688 --> 00:05:24.950
Do you think it's a trap?

00:05:25.056 --> 00:05:26.683
Do I think Seska is capable

00:05:26.724 --> 00:05:29.056
of manipulating
you and me with this?

00:05:29.093 --> 00:05:31.118
Oh, yes.

00:05:31.162 --> 00:05:33.687
On the other hand,
it was time for her to deliver.

00:05:33.731 --> 00:05:34.720
And that baby we saw

00:05:34.766 --> 00:05:36.825
did look part Cardassian
and part human.

00:05:36.868 --> 00:05:39.336
And knowing Culluh,
I'm sure his pride was wounded

00:05:39.370 --> 00:05:41.395
when he realized
the child wasn't his.

00:05:41.439 --> 00:05:42.963
It makes sense, Chakotay.

00:05:43.074 --> 00:05:45.599
It might all be true.

00:05:45.643 --> 00:05:46.701
Still, the safest thing would be

00:05:46.744 --> 00:05:49.372
to ignore this message
and resume our course.

00:05:51.149 --> 00:05:53.208
I'm not going to resume
our course just yet.

00:05:53.251 --> 00:05:55.811
I want you to think about it,
Chakotay.

00:05:57.922 --> 00:06:00.288
This has to be your decision.

00:06:00.325 --> 00:06:03.192
If you choose to go after him,

00:06:03.227 --> 00:06:04.854
I know I speak
for the entire crew...

00:06:04.896 --> 00:06:06.921
Starfleet and Maquis alike...

00:06:06.998 --> 00:06:09.831
when I say
we'll stand behind you.

00:06:24.649 --> 00:06:27.140
Ah-koo-chee-moya.

00:06:27.185 --> 00:06:31.952
We are far from the sacred
places of our grandfathers.

00:06:31.990 --> 00:06:35.323
We are far from the bones
of my people,

00:06:35.360 --> 00:06:39.353
but I ask on this day
of sorrow and uncertainty

00:06:39.397 --> 00:06:43.959
that the wisdom
of my father find me

00:06:44.035 --> 00:06:47.368
and help me understand
my dilemma.

00:06:47.405 --> 00:06:51.102
Speak to me, Father.

00:06:51.142 --> 00:06:54.475
Speak to me in my dreams.

00:06:54.512 --> 00:06:57.845
I've never seen you
so troubled, Chakotay.

00:07:29.714 --> 00:07:31.739
I have a son, Father.

00:07:33.084 --> 00:07:35.177
A son, Chakotay?

00:07:36.287 --> 00:07:38.346
Oh.

00:07:38.389 --> 00:07:41.586
This is the reason
for your despair.

00:07:41.626 --> 00:07:45.892
Was he born with two arms
and two legs

00:07:45.930 --> 00:07:48.262
and a heart that beats?

00:07:48.299 --> 00:07:49.425
Yes, but...

00:07:49.467 --> 00:07:51.958
Then it's a cause
for celebration.

00:07:52.036 --> 00:07:56.803
You will make a fine father.

00:07:56.841 --> 00:07:58.604
You needn't worry.

00:08:00.545 --> 00:08:03.241
I'm not sure I'm willing
to be a father to him.

00:08:03.281 --> 00:08:05.909
Hmm. Not willing?

00:08:06.017 --> 00:08:09.009
He was born without my consent.

00:08:09.053 --> 00:08:10.452
I had no part in it.

00:08:12.123 --> 00:08:14.216
No part in it?

00:08:14.258 --> 00:08:17.659
Well, it's been a long time,
so forgive me,

00:08:17.695 --> 00:08:21.529
but it seems that I had
to play a part

00:08:21.566 --> 00:08:23.591
before your mother
could conceive.

00:08:23.634 --> 00:08:26.603
My DNA was taken from me.

00:08:26.637 --> 00:08:28.696
Used by a woman
to impregnate herself

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:30.037
without my permission.

00:08:32.043 --> 00:08:33.943
I see.

00:08:34.045 --> 00:08:36.377
You're trying to decide
whether you should

00:08:36.414 --> 00:08:38.439
accept the child
in your heart.

00:08:38.483 --> 00:08:40.576
It's more than that.

00:08:40.618 --> 00:08:42.415
But it must begin with that.

00:08:42.453 --> 00:08:44.580
How do you take
a child into your heart

00:08:44.622 --> 00:08:47.523
who is forced upon you
by a mother's deception?

00:08:50.928 --> 00:08:53.055
He knows nothing of deception.

00:08:54.365 --> 00:08:56.196
He is innocent.

00:08:57.735 --> 00:09:00.533
Centuries ago,
when the women of our tribe

00:09:00.571 --> 00:09:04.632
were raped
by white conquerors, many

00:09:04.675 --> 00:09:06.870
gave birth to their children.

00:09:06.911 --> 00:09:09.880
And we did not reject them.

00:09:09.914 --> 00:09:12.906
They were accepted by the tribe.

00:09:14.385 --> 00:09:17.548
One was a direct ancestor
of ours, Chakotay.

00:09:17.588 --> 00:09:22.048
His name was Ce Acatl.

00:09:22.093 --> 00:09:25.927
He became a great leader
of our people.

00:09:25.963 --> 00:09:32.027
Here is a man who was given life
without his mother's consent.

00:09:32.069 --> 00:09:34.435
Are you so different from her?

00:09:35.973 --> 00:09:38.999
And is your child so different
from Ce Acatl?

00:09:44.148 --> 00:09:45.479
No.

00:09:48.586 --> 00:09:51.384
He is your son, Chakotay.

00:09:52.857 --> 00:09:55.553
And he is a child of our people.

00:10:19.884 --> 00:10:20.976
I've been in touch

00:10:21.085 --> 00:10:24.077
with the Talaxian
mining colony on Prema II.

00:10:24.121 --> 00:10:26.214
They're willing to come
to our assistance

00:10:26.257 --> 00:10:27.349
if we run into trouble.

00:10:27.391 --> 00:10:31.157
That's good for about 40 hours
if we average warp 2.

00:10:31.195 --> 00:10:32.958
After that, we're out
of their com range.

00:10:32.997 --> 00:10:34.988
Well, it's nice to know
we have friends in the area.

00:10:35.032 --> 00:10:36.124
Thank you, Neelix.

00:10:36.167 --> 00:10:38.465
I recommend a full diagnostic
of our tactical array

00:10:38.502 --> 00:10:40.094
prior to the start
of the mission, Captain.

00:10:40.137 --> 00:10:42.002
Agreed, but I want more
from tactical, Lieutenant.

00:10:42.106 --> 00:10:43.903
I want to anticipate a trap.

00:10:43.941 --> 00:10:46.569
And I want a few tricks up
our sleeves, if we need them.

00:10:46.611 --> 00:10:50.012
Captain, I could program the
deflector grid to make it look

00:10:50.081 --> 00:10:51.343
like we have help on the way.

00:10:51.382 --> 00:10:52.542
I'll show you what I mean.

00:10:52.583 --> 00:10:54.244
Excuse me, Doctor.

00:10:57.688 --> 00:10:58.655
Echo displacement.

00:10:58.689 --> 00:11:00.020
Exactly.

00:11:00.124 --> 00:11:02.456
This is how we'd look
to the enemy sensors.

00:11:03.961 --> 00:11:07.419
If we generate multiple
decoy images like these,

00:11:07.465 --> 00:11:10.832
the Kazon would think that
ships are coming toward us.

00:11:10.868 --> 00:11:12.267
We could create
as many as we want.

00:11:12.303 --> 00:11:14.066
That's a good start, Harry.

00:11:14.105 --> 00:11:15.595
It should distract them
for a while.

00:11:15.640 --> 00:11:16.698
But what else can we do

00:11:16.741 --> 00:11:19.335
if we're eventually intercepted
by a superior force?

00:11:19.377 --> 00:11:21.675
If you don't mind,
I do have something to add.

00:11:23.247 --> 00:11:24.680
Thank you.

00:11:24.715 --> 00:11:26.740
Captain, I hesitate
to offer suggestions

00:11:26.784 --> 00:11:28.513
in a field of endeavor
that is not

00:11:28.552 --> 00:11:30.315
within my usual area
of expertise.

00:11:30.354 --> 00:11:31.844
Please, Doctor, your suggestions

00:11:31.889 --> 00:11:33.550
on any subject
are always welcome.

00:11:33.591 --> 00:11:36.958
Really? In that case,
you may expect several more

00:11:36.994 --> 00:11:38.962
on a variety of matters
in the near future.

00:11:38.996 --> 00:11:41.897
Right now, may I suggest
that we also consider

00:11:41.933 --> 00:11:45.300
attempting to create
an actual holographic illusion

00:11:45.336 --> 00:11:47.236
of friendly ships.

00:11:47.271 --> 00:11:48.499
With all due respect, Doctor,

00:11:48.539 --> 00:11:51.406
we can't even figure out how
to project you into this room.

00:11:51.442 --> 00:11:54.275
How are we supposed to create
holographic ships in space?

00:11:54.312 --> 00:11:55.301
I would humbly submit

00:11:55.346 --> 00:11:57.280
that my program
is far more sophisticated

00:11:57.315 --> 00:11:59.016
than your run-of-the-mill
hologram.

00:11:59.149 --> 00:12:01.276
In fact, projecting the illusion

00:12:01.318 --> 00:12:03.445
of a large
three-dimensional object

00:12:03.487 --> 00:12:05.717
has been a trick of magicians
for centuries.

00:12:05.756 --> 00:12:07.849
We'll just do it with mirrors.

00:12:07.891 --> 00:12:10.860
Mr. Paris' predictable attempts
at humor not withstanding,

00:12:10.894 --> 00:12:13.328
that is precisely
what I would suggest.

00:12:13.363 --> 00:12:17.561
Installing holo-emitters along
the hull with parabolic mirrors

00:12:17.601 --> 00:12:20.502
to enlarge the images as they
are reflected into space.

00:12:20.537 --> 00:12:21.595
We're going to use up

00:12:21.638 --> 00:12:24.232
a lot of our power reserves
trying to pull it off.

00:12:24.274 --> 00:12:27.641
If these ships can fool
the Kazon, it's worth it.

00:12:27.677 --> 00:12:29.144
But can they?

00:12:29.179 --> 00:12:31.670
If the Kazon
scan the holograms, they will

00:12:31.715 --> 00:12:34.445
immediately realize there
are no life signs on board,

00:12:34.484 --> 00:12:35.473
no power signatures...

00:12:35.519 --> 00:12:37.180
Okay, so we can't
fool them for long,

00:12:37.220 --> 00:12:38.653
but maybe it'll be long enough.

00:12:38.688 --> 00:12:39.985
It's an advantage.

00:12:40.023 --> 00:12:42.389
And we'll need every advantage
we can get on this mission.

00:12:42.426 --> 00:12:43.916
Work on the Doctor with it,
B'Elanna.

00:12:43.960 --> 00:12:45.860
Mr. Kim, cut power
to all systems

00:12:45.896 --> 00:12:47.363
to minimum requirements.

00:12:47.397 --> 00:12:48.489
I don't want to show up

00:12:48.532 --> 00:12:50.124
on any Kazon
long-range scanners.

00:12:50.167 --> 00:12:53.000
Mr. Paris, locate the warp
signature from Culluh's ship

00:12:53.036 --> 00:12:54.594
and set a course to follow...
warp 2.

00:12:54.638 --> 00:12:55.605
Aye, Captain.

00:12:55.639 --> 00:12:56.799
Dismissed.

00:12:56.840 --> 00:12:59.832
Uh, excuse me,
but there is one more thing.

00:13:01.445 --> 00:13:02.912
Thank you.

00:13:17.527 --> 00:13:18.858
It's not Culluh's ship.

00:13:18.895 --> 00:13:20.294
Looks more like a shuttle.

00:13:20.330 --> 00:13:21.297
Slow to impulse.

00:13:21.331 --> 00:13:22.923
Set an intercept course,
Mr. Paris.

00:13:22.966 --> 00:13:25.560
Have they indicated
the nature of the distress?

00:13:25.602 --> 00:13:27.229
Just a signal, Captain.
No response to our hails.

00:13:27.270 --> 00:13:28.464
Let's go to Red Alert.

00:13:29.606 --> 00:13:30.573
Visual range.

00:13:30.607 --> 00:13:31.767
On screen.

00:13:33.343 --> 00:13:36.107
Showing one life sign.
Adult Kazon male.

00:13:36.146 --> 00:13:37.340
He's in critical condition.

00:13:37.380 --> 00:13:38.347
Janeway to Sick Bay.

00:13:38.381 --> 00:13:40.349
Prepare to receive
an emergency transport.

00:13:40.383 --> 00:13:41.407
Standing by, Captain.

00:13:41.451 --> 00:13:42.418
Commander.

00:13:42.452 --> 00:13:43.817
Mr. Tuvok, you have the Bridge.

00:13:43.854 --> 00:13:44.821
Remain at Red Alert.

00:13:44.855 --> 00:13:46.049
Aye, Captain.

00:13:49.392 --> 00:13:50.484
His hip is broken.

00:13:50.527 --> 00:13:52.927
Showing severe inflammation
in the bronchial tissue.

00:13:52.963 --> 00:13:54.555
It appears he inhaled
noxious gases

00:13:54.598 --> 00:13:56.156
vented in the damaged shuttle.

00:13:56.199 --> 00:13:57.826
40 milligrams pulmozine.

00:13:57.868 --> 00:13:58.960
I know this man.

00:13:59.002 --> 00:14:00.435
His name's Tierna.

00:14:00.470 --> 00:14:02.131
He's one of Seska's aides.

00:14:02.172 --> 00:14:04.106
She had him work me over
when I was on their ship.

00:14:05.442 --> 00:14:09.242
Seska... is dead.

00:14:21.158 --> 00:14:23.649
Seska thought that she
could manipulate the maje.

00:14:23.693 --> 00:14:26.355
She bragged about it to me
more than once,

00:14:26.396 --> 00:14:28.261
but this time she was wrong.

00:14:28.298 --> 00:14:32.564
We had just launched the buoy
with the message for you.

00:14:32.602 --> 00:14:35.093
Then they came for her.

00:14:35.138 --> 00:14:40.405
They cut her throat,
as Culluh watched.

00:14:40.443 --> 00:14:45.346
He ordered them to execute me,
but I bribed one of the guards

00:14:45.382 --> 00:14:47.077
to get me to a shuttle.

00:14:47.117 --> 00:14:50.450
As soon as he saw it leaving,
Culluh opened fire...

00:14:50.487 --> 00:14:53.718
destroyed
my life-support systems.

00:14:53.757 --> 00:14:56.624
He left me in space to die.

00:14:56.660 --> 00:14:58.252
What about the child?

00:14:58.295 --> 00:15:03.892
Taken to the Gema IV colony
to be raised as a servant.

00:15:03.934 --> 00:15:06.926
We'll be needing your help
getting to the Gema system.

00:15:07.003 --> 00:15:09.062
You're going after him?

00:15:09.105 --> 00:15:11.665
This ship, alone?

00:15:11.708 --> 00:15:14.700
I want nothing to do with this.

00:15:14.744 --> 00:15:17.508
I'm not taking you
into Nistrim space.

00:15:19.015 --> 00:15:22.041
Under the circumstances, I'd say
you don't have much of a choice.

00:15:26.957 --> 00:15:28.219
What's his prognosis?

00:15:28.258 --> 00:15:31.227
He'll be on his feet
in a day or two,

00:15:31.261 --> 00:15:32.728
but there's still
a number of things

00:15:32.762 --> 00:15:33.854
we need to keep an eye on.

00:15:33.897 --> 00:15:39.358
He's had... a nasty concussion,
spinal cord trauma

00:15:39.402 --> 00:15:43.736
and a polycythemia, the cause
of which I've yet to discover.

00:15:43.773 --> 00:15:45.297
Polycythemia?

00:15:45.342 --> 00:15:48.834
An abnormal increase in the
number of red blood cells.

00:15:50.313 --> 00:15:52.577
I'd like you to run
an autonomic response analysis

00:15:52.616 --> 00:15:53.981
the next time I question him.

00:15:54.017 --> 00:15:56.110
I'm afraid
that won't help you determine

00:15:56.152 --> 00:15:57.414
if he's telling the truth,
Commander.

00:15:57.454 --> 00:16:00.582
An ARA depends on making
a baseline comparison

00:16:00.624 --> 00:16:03.559
with a known response
for a given species.

00:16:03.593 --> 00:16:04.617
Any Tom, Dick or Harry

00:16:04.661 --> 00:16:06.788
from the Alpha Quadrant,
I could probably help you,

00:16:06.830 --> 00:16:09.663
but not with any of the new
species of the Delta Quadrant.

00:16:13.303 --> 00:16:15.703
Regarding his veracity,
it may help you to know

00:16:15.739 --> 00:16:17.400
that if we'd arrived
an hour later,

00:16:17.440 --> 00:16:20.068
he would have been dead
from his injuries.

00:16:24.214 --> 00:16:26.375
The molecular variance residual
on his shuttle

00:16:26.416 --> 00:16:29.408
is evidence of disruptor blasts,
and the signature is Kazon,

00:16:29.452 --> 00:16:32.319
so at least that part of
his story seems to be true.

00:16:32.355 --> 00:16:34.789
Plus, we confirmed
nitrogen tetroxide fumes

00:16:34.824 --> 00:16:35.882
were in the cabin.

00:16:35.925 --> 00:16:37.859
If all this was part
of a Kazon scheme,

00:16:37.894 --> 00:16:39.657
he had to be willing
to breathe poison

00:16:39.696 --> 00:16:41.095
for hours before we got there.

00:16:41.131 --> 00:16:42.530
Have you found anything at all

00:16:42.565 --> 00:16:44.226
that would cast
doubt on his story?

00:16:46.303 --> 00:16:47.930
No.

00:16:50.674 --> 00:16:52.437
I still don't trust him.

00:16:56.112 --> 00:16:58.137
The trip would take six days
at warp 2.

00:16:58.181 --> 00:17:01.878
Four days, if you didn't take
such a circuitous route...

00:17:01.918 --> 00:17:03.909
if we simply went
across the Tenarus cluster.

00:17:03.953 --> 00:17:05.079
You would encounter

00:17:05.121 --> 00:17:08.750
the Nistrim fleet
before a single day passed.

00:17:08.792 --> 00:17:10.555
Anyone who knows
this part of space

00:17:10.593 --> 00:17:12.151
will tell you the same thing.

00:17:12.195 --> 00:17:14.891
It so happens that I do know

00:17:14.931 --> 00:17:17.695
this part of space,
my Kazon friend.

00:17:17.734 --> 00:17:20.259
I just wanted to see if you
would tell us the truth.

00:17:20.303 --> 00:17:23.363
The route he suggests
is safer, Captain.

00:17:23.406 --> 00:17:24.737
Of course it's safer.

00:17:24.774 --> 00:17:28.210
I don't want to run into Culluh
any more than you do.

00:17:28.244 --> 00:17:30.804
We might have more
success avoiding him

00:17:30.847 --> 00:17:34.010
if you gave us the command codes
for the Nistrim defense net.

00:17:36.119 --> 00:17:39.850
Computer, display tactical
overview of our current course.

00:17:43.927 --> 00:17:51.197
Enter code sequence: Four-nine-
one-one-seven-zero-Culluh.

00:17:58.341 --> 00:18:01.902
Mr. Paris, adjust our course
to avoid the defense net.

00:18:01.945 --> 00:18:03.276
Aye, Captain.

00:18:03.313 --> 00:18:06.441
That is not an end
to the danger.

00:18:06.483 --> 00:18:09.577
We are heading
into an area of space

00:18:09.619 --> 00:18:13.919
populated by Kazon factions
that are loyal to no one.

00:18:13.990 --> 00:18:17.790
They will attack
without provocation.

00:18:25.235 --> 00:18:29.638
Vessel approaching.
Coordinates: 314 mark 21.

00:18:29.672 --> 00:18:31.230
Signature is Kazon.

00:18:31.274 --> 00:18:32.366
Red Alert.

00:18:32.409 --> 00:18:34.934
Configuration
of the ship, Mr. Tuvok?

00:18:34.978 --> 00:18:36.411
A small raider, Captain.

00:18:36.446 --> 00:18:38.073
It does not pose
a significant threat.

00:18:38.114 --> 00:18:41.515
Nevertheless, it is powering up
its weapon systems.

00:18:43.286 --> 00:18:44.378
Shields are holding.

00:18:45.822 --> 00:18:46.914
Return fire.

00:18:53.228 --> 00:18:54.525
The raider is breaking
off its attack.

00:18:54.563 --> 00:18:55.689
Minor damage

00:18:55.730 --> 00:18:58.893
to secondary command
processors on Deck 12.

00:18:58.934 --> 00:19:00.162
EPS power supplies,

00:19:00.202 --> 00:19:02.762
and isolinear controllers
are off-line.

00:19:02.804 --> 00:19:03.771
No casualties though.

00:19:03.805 --> 00:19:05.670
Begin repairs, Mr. Kim.

00:19:05.707 --> 00:19:07.902
Any other sign of Kazon ships,
Lieutenant?

00:19:08.009 --> 00:19:09.306
Nothing on long-range sensors.

00:19:09.344 --> 00:19:10.902
The raider is
continuing to retreat.

00:19:11.012 --> 00:19:14.311
We should have a couple of hours
to ourselves at least.

00:19:14.349 --> 00:19:15.475
Good. We can use them.

00:19:15.517 --> 00:19:16.848
Stand down Red Alert.

00:19:16.885 --> 00:19:18.443
Captain, we're about to go

00:19:18.487 --> 00:19:21.547
beyond the com range
of the Talaxian colony.

00:19:21.590 --> 00:19:23.148
Just thought you'd like to know.

00:19:23.191 --> 00:19:25.056
Thank you, Lieutenant.

00:19:25.093 --> 00:19:26.390
Maintain current course.

00:19:26.428 --> 00:19:27.417
Captain.

00:19:29.698 --> 00:19:31.529
I haven't forgotten, Mr. Tuvok.

00:19:31.566 --> 00:19:32.533
Very well.

00:19:32.567 --> 00:19:33.966
This seems
as good a time as any.

00:19:45.347 --> 00:19:46.314
Captain.

00:19:46.348 --> 00:19:47.315
Mr. Suder.

00:19:47.349 --> 00:19:49.510
Please... please come in.

00:19:49.551 --> 00:19:50.950
W-won't you sit down?

00:19:50.986 --> 00:19:52.715
Excuse the mess.

00:19:52.754 --> 00:19:55.746
I wasn't expecting company.

00:19:55.790 --> 00:19:58.588
Can I get you some tea?

00:19:58.627 --> 00:20:00.117
Have you had lunch?

00:20:00.162 --> 00:20:01.686
Nothing, thank you.

00:20:01.730 --> 00:20:04.631
Lieutenant Tuvok has been
telling me about your progress.

00:20:04.666 --> 00:20:08.067
Has he? Well, I'm...

00:20:08.103 --> 00:20:10.697
I'm very grateful to him,
Captain.

00:20:10.739 --> 00:20:12.366
I still have a lot
to learn, of course,

00:20:12.407 --> 00:20:13.965
but he is an excellent tutor.

00:20:14.009 --> 00:20:16.102
When we first started
our studies, I...

00:20:16.144 --> 00:20:18.874
The Captain's time
is limited, Mr. Suder.

00:20:18.914 --> 00:20:20.506
What?

00:20:20.549 --> 00:20:22.278
Oh.

00:20:22.317 --> 00:20:23.477
Of course.

00:20:23.518 --> 00:20:25.645
I have explained
your proposal to her.

00:20:25.687 --> 00:20:27.587
I'd like to know
more about it, Mr. Suder.

00:20:27.622 --> 00:20:29.089
What exactly would be involved?

00:20:29.124 --> 00:20:31.490
Yes, yes...

00:20:31.526 --> 00:20:33.118
Let me show you.

00:20:33.161 --> 00:20:36.824
I've actually had
very encouraging results

00:20:36.865 --> 00:20:39.333
with a new
gene-splicing technique.

00:20:39.367 --> 00:20:42.598
I created a targeted
restriction enzyme

00:20:42.637 --> 00:20:44.332
to facilitate the hybrid.

00:20:44.372 --> 00:20:45.964
And you feel
you could experiment

00:20:46.007 --> 00:20:48.771
on our airponic crops
here in your quarters?

00:20:48.810 --> 00:20:52.940
Absolutely. I would make
this an airponic laboratory

00:20:52.981 --> 00:20:55.745
and all I would need
are a few plants,

00:20:55.784 --> 00:20:57.012
certain chemicals and equipment.

00:20:57.085 --> 00:20:58.484
What sort of chemicals
and equipment?

00:20:58.520 --> 00:20:59.919
Nothing dangerous.

00:20:59.955 --> 00:21:02.321
I've prepared a list.

00:21:10.298 --> 00:21:12.766
It's an interesting
proposition, Mr. Suder.

00:21:12.801 --> 00:21:14.826
Let me discuss it with Kes
and Lieutenant Tuvok

00:21:14.869 --> 00:21:15.961
and I'll get back to you.

00:21:16.037 --> 00:21:17.629
I've already discussed
it with Kes

00:21:17.672 --> 00:21:20.766
and she is very interested.

00:21:20.809 --> 00:21:22.572
Good. Let me give it
some thought.

00:21:22.611 --> 00:21:24.772
If you're worried
you can't trust me, Captain...

00:21:24.813 --> 00:21:25.905
Mr. Tuvok has assured...

00:21:25.947 --> 00:21:30.281
I only want to do something...
something for the ship.

00:21:30.318 --> 00:21:32.513
I understand, Mr. Suder.

00:21:32.554 --> 00:21:33.748
Then what's the problem?

00:21:33.788 --> 00:21:35.449
Why won't you give me an answer?

00:21:35.490 --> 00:21:36.684
Mr. Suder.

00:21:43.465 --> 00:21:46.559
I just want to do
something for the ship.

00:21:49.237 --> 00:21:50.568
Excuse me.

00:22:06.988 --> 00:22:09.047
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:22:09.090 --> 00:22:12.389
None of the four Kazon attacks
have caused serious damage,

00:22:12.427 --> 00:22:14.918
but the starboard ventral
has been hit each time...

00:22:14.963 --> 00:22:18.228
complicating repairs on the
secondary command processors.

00:22:22.437 --> 00:22:24.962
You are making an adequate
recovery, Mr. Tierna.

00:22:25.073 --> 00:22:27.132
The only matter
that I simply cannot understand

00:22:27.175 --> 00:22:28.802
is this lingering polycythemia.

00:22:28.843 --> 00:22:30.242
I feel fine.

00:22:30.278 --> 00:22:31.404
The medical record you gave us

00:22:31.446 --> 00:22:34.108
does not indicate any prior
blood disorders.

00:22:34.149 --> 00:22:35.946
Might it be an inherited trait?

00:22:35.984 --> 00:22:37.383
Do you know
if your parents ever?

00:22:37.419 --> 00:22:40.547
My parents were killed
in a Trabe attack

00:22:40.588 --> 00:22:42.783
shortly after I was born.

00:22:44.292 --> 00:22:45.623
I see.

00:22:45.660 --> 00:22:48.527
Well, we'll need to monitor
this condition for a while.

00:22:48.563 --> 00:22:50.690
It might be due to some
chemical imbalance

00:22:50.732 --> 00:22:52.222
that our sensors
aren't recognizing.

00:22:52.267 --> 00:22:54.167
Possibly the result

00:22:54.202 --> 00:22:56.602
of the toxins you inhaled
while on the shuttle.

00:22:59.040 --> 00:23:00.200
You're welcome.

00:23:06.014 --> 00:23:07.242
Feeling better?

00:23:07.282 --> 00:23:10.183
I'm sure I'll make
a complete recovery.

00:23:10.218 --> 00:23:12.550
Just in time for the Gema
colony's defense force

00:23:12.587 --> 00:23:14.350
to destroy us all.

00:23:14.389 --> 00:23:16.949
You're still not optimistic
about our chances, are you?

00:23:17.025 --> 00:23:18.083
No.

00:23:18.126 --> 00:23:20.356
We've had no problem
repelling the attacks so far.

00:23:20.395 --> 00:23:23.421
Attacks... when there's
a real Nistrim attack,

00:23:23.465 --> 00:23:24.796
you'll know it.

00:23:24.833 --> 00:23:27.768
You still have pride in the
Nistrim, don't you, Tierna?

00:23:27.802 --> 00:23:29.360
Even after what they did to you.

00:23:29.404 --> 00:23:31.964
I remember that pride
in your eyes when you

00:23:32.006 --> 00:23:34.873
pounded me with your fists
while I was tied to a chair.

00:23:34.909 --> 00:23:37.605
And I can see it
in your eyes now,

00:23:37.645 --> 00:23:40.978
and that scares
the hell out of me.

00:23:41.049 --> 00:23:44.576
You must scare easily,
Federation.

00:23:47.422 --> 00:23:49.185
Tell me something, Tierna.

00:23:49.224 --> 00:23:52.216
Every Kazon attack seems to
focus on our starboard ventral.

00:23:52.260 --> 00:23:53.989
Think that might be
some kind of pattern?

00:23:54.062 --> 00:23:55.324
I wouldn't know.

00:23:55.363 --> 00:23:58.127
Because if it is,
and you've been lying to us...

00:23:58.166 --> 00:23:59.793
Commander Chakotay.

00:23:59.834 --> 00:24:02.667
Not in my Sick Bay, please.

00:24:13.214 --> 00:24:14.738
Firing phasers.

00:24:14.783 --> 00:24:16.114
Increase speed
to one-half impulse.

00:24:16.151 --> 00:24:17.118
Aye, Captain.

00:24:17.152 --> 00:24:19.518
They're coming
at our starboard ventral again.

00:24:19.554 --> 00:24:21.078
Our shields there
haven't been repaired yet.

00:24:21.122 --> 00:24:22.316
We're going to sustain
more damage

00:24:22.357 --> 00:24:23.688
to the secondary
command processors.

00:24:23.725 --> 00:24:25.090
Starboard ventral.

00:24:25.126 --> 00:24:27.117
Warning.
Fires have been detected

00:24:27.162 --> 00:24:31.428
on Decks 12 and 15
Sections A-4 through C-18.

00:24:31.466 --> 00:24:32.933
Control units are responding,
Captain.

00:24:32.967 --> 00:24:35.765
Keep our port forequarter facing
the line of attack, Mr. Paris.

00:24:35.804 --> 00:24:37.271
Don't let them see
our starboard ventral.

00:24:37.305 --> 00:24:38.397
I'm doing my best.

00:24:38.440 --> 00:24:40.431
Continuous fire,
starboard phasers.

00:24:40.475 --> 00:24:42.238
Acknowledged.

00:24:42.277 --> 00:24:43.574
They're withdrawing, Captain.

00:24:43.611 --> 00:24:44.805
Stand down Red Alert.

00:24:46.648 --> 00:24:48.206
Mr. Kim?

00:24:48.249 --> 00:24:50.376
Deck 12 is in shambles.

00:24:50.418 --> 00:24:51.783
We barely have time
to begin repairs

00:24:51.820 --> 00:24:53.082
before they attack it again.

00:24:53.121 --> 00:24:54.713
At least no one was hurt.

00:24:54.756 --> 00:24:57.384
The secondary command processors
are nonfunctional.

00:24:57.425 --> 00:24:58.790
We'll have to rebuild them.

00:24:58.827 --> 00:25:00.454
I'd say we're looking
at two days' work

00:25:00.495 --> 00:25:02.190
if we're not attacked again.

00:25:02.230 --> 00:25:04.255
Why would these factions
of Kazon, loyal to no one,

00:25:04.299 --> 00:25:05.857
all have the same agenda?

00:25:05.900 --> 00:25:08.130
And why would that agenda
focus on a nonessential

00:25:08.169 --> 00:25:09.227
area of the ship?

00:25:09.270 --> 00:25:10.237
I don't know, but it feels

00:25:10.271 --> 00:25:11.932
like we're being pecked
to death by ducks.

00:25:12.006 --> 00:25:13.940
We can't just stay on this
course and wait to see

00:25:14.008 --> 00:25:15.236
what they have in store for us.

00:25:15.276 --> 00:25:17.676
I agree. It's time
to reexamine our game plan.

00:25:17.712 --> 00:25:19.304
Mr. Paris, reverse course.

00:25:19.347 --> 00:25:20.609
Aye, Captain.

00:25:20.648 --> 00:25:22.377
Mr. Tierna should be
restricted to quarters

00:25:22.417 --> 00:25:23.714
on a secured deck
until further notice.

00:25:23.751 --> 00:25:25.912
Acknowledged.

00:25:45.139 --> 00:25:46.970
Dinnertime, Mr. Suder.

00:25:47.008 --> 00:25:50.409
We have
a fine leola root soup tonight.

00:25:53.548 --> 00:25:55.743
I'm not hungry.

00:26:00.687 --> 00:26:02.314
Red Alert.

00:26:02.355 --> 00:26:03.549
I'm afraid we have to go.

00:26:03.590 --> 00:26:05.524
I'll leave it here.

00:26:08.728 --> 00:26:10.593
Just in case.

00:26:15.635 --> 00:26:17.296
How many do you count,
Mr. Tuvok?

00:26:17.337 --> 00:26:20.932
Eight large carrier vessels,
confirmed Kazon signatures.

00:26:21.007 --> 00:26:23.498
Funny how they show up
right after we reverse course.

00:26:23.543 --> 00:26:24.532
Time to intercept?

00:26:24.578 --> 00:26:25.772
Eight minutes.

00:26:25.812 --> 00:26:28.872
Their attack formation is
a classic Cardassian echelon.

00:26:28.915 --> 00:26:29.882
Curious.

00:26:29.916 --> 00:26:30.940
They have left us

00:26:31.017 --> 00:26:33.417
with an obvious avenue
of escape, Captain.

00:26:36.389 --> 00:26:38.323
You're right.
It is curious.

00:26:38.358 --> 00:26:40.553
Too curious for me.

00:26:40.594 --> 00:26:43.119
I don't know what's down
that avenue of escape,

00:26:43.163 --> 00:26:45.723
Mr. Tuvok, but I like
to choose my own way.

00:26:45.765 --> 00:26:48.063
Set a course
to intercept their lead ship.

00:26:48.101 --> 00:26:49.591
Aye, Captain.

00:26:50.637 --> 00:26:52.400
Battle stations.

00:27:05.085 --> 00:27:06.313
Time to intercept?

00:27:06.353 --> 00:27:08.048
Three minutes, ten seconds...

00:27:08.088 --> 00:27:09.783
give or take a photon torpedo.

00:27:09.823 --> 00:27:10.721
Mr. Kim?

00:27:14.527 --> 00:27:16.552
Echo displacement ready,
Captain.

00:27:16.596 --> 00:27:18.120
Send in the cavalry.

00:27:18.164 --> 00:27:19.961
Activating deflector grid.

00:27:23.003 --> 00:27:25.836
They should be seeing the same
thing on their scanners...

00:27:25.872 --> 00:27:27.737
ten ships
with Talaxian signatures.

00:27:27.774 --> 00:27:29.867
Four of the Kazon ships
are breaking formation.

00:27:29.909 --> 00:27:31.774
Confirmed.
They're changing course.

00:27:31.811 --> 00:27:33.073
They took the bait.

00:27:33.113 --> 00:27:34.842
That only leaves four
for us to handle.

00:27:34.881 --> 00:27:36.280
I like those odds better
than eight to one.

00:27:36.316 --> 00:27:37.283
Two minutes to intercept.

00:27:37.317 --> 00:27:39.217
Janeway to Torres.

00:27:39.252 --> 00:27:40.947
We're ready down here, Captain.

00:27:40.987 --> 00:27:43.217
All the new holo-projectors
are on line.

00:27:43.256 --> 00:27:44.951
We can create
three Talaxian ships

00:27:45.025 --> 00:27:46.287
whenever you want to.

00:27:46.326 --> 00:27:48.726
In about a minute and a half,
B'Elanna. Stand by.

00:27:48.762 --> 00:27:51.526
Perhaps we should try
one last systems check.

00:27:51.564 --> 00:27:53.259
We've already done it twice.

00:27:53.300 --> 00:27:55.427
I'm new at this,
and we've never put

00:27:55.468 --> 00:27:57.800
such a demand on
the holo-generators before.

00:27:57.837 --> 00:27:59.805
We should've boosted
the power input.

00:27:59.839 --> 00:28:02.307
The defense systems are going
to need all the auxiliary power

00:28:02.342 --> 00:28:03.832
we have, Doctor.

00:28:03.877 --> 00:28:05.139
We might try a preliminary...

00:28:05.178 --> 00:28:06.611
Doctor!

00:28:06.646 --> 00:28:08.409
Lt'll work.

00:28:08.448 --> 00:28:09.881
Everything'll be fine.

00:28:09.916 --> 00:28:11.349
I'm not worried.

00:28:15.221 --> 00:28:17.155
Here we go.

00:28:17.190 --> 00:28:19.385
They are randomly detonating
torpedoes in our flight path.

00:28:19.426 --> 00:28:21.485
Shields are holding.
No damage.

00:28:21.528 --> 00:28:23.052
Hold your fire, Mr. Tuvok.

00:28:23.096 --> 00:28:25.360
They may have torpedoes
to waste... we don't.

00:28:25.398 --> 00:28:27.298
30 seconds to intercept.

00:28:27.334 --> 00:28:28.892
Take us out of warp.

00:28:28.935 --> 00:28:30.061
Engaging impulse engines.

00:28:30.103 --> 00:28:31.593
Power to all weapon systems.

00:28:31.638 --> 00:28:32.832
Stand by phasers.

00:28:32.872 --> 00:28:35.602
Kazon vessel, 10,000 kilometers
off our starboard bow.

00:28:35.642 --> 00:28:36.666
Not yet.

00:28:36.710 --> 00:28:37.768
6,000 kilometers.

00:28:37.811 --> 00:28:38.869
Not yet.

00:28:38.912 --> 00:28:40.539
5,000.

00:28:40.580 --> 00:28:42.309
3,000... 2,000.

00:28:42.349 --> 00:28:43.646
Now!

00:28:50.190 --> 00:28:52.784
Initiating evasive maneuvers,
beta sequence.

00:28:52.826 --> 00:28:54.623
Two more
Kazon ships approaching.

00:28:55.528 --> 00:28:56.893
Shields at 90 percent.

00:29:05.905 --> 00:29:08.339
Janeway to Torres.
Initiate holo-programs.

00:29:08.375 --> 00:29:09.740
Acknowledged.

00:29:09.776 --> 00:29:11.004
Energizing.

00:29:23.056 --> 00:29:24.489
That's two.

00:29:24.524 --> 00:29:26.287
And here's number three.

00:29:32.665 --> 00:29:36.795
Help! Man overboard!

00:29:49.549 --> 00:29:51.073
Doctor, are you there?

00:29:51.117 --> 00:29:52.846
Are you all right?

00:29:52.886 --> 00:29:56.913
I told you we should have run
one last systems check.

00:30:02.562 --> 00:30:03.620
Fourth Kazon ship, dead ahead.

00:30:03.663 --> 00:30:05.494
But they're dividing
their fire, Captain.

00:30:05.532 --> 00:30:06.829
The holograms are working.

00:30:06.866 --> 00:30:07.924
Ready photons.

00:30:07.967 --> 00:30:08.956
Torpedoes loaded.

00:30:09.002 --> 00:30:10.629
Take us about, Mr. Paris.

00:30:10.670 --> 00:30:12.661
We want a good angle
on that fourth ship.

00:30:12.705 --> 00:30:15.902
Coming about, 141 mark 20.

00:30:15.942 --> 00:30:17.807
Fire photon number one.

00:30:20.346 --> 00:30:21.472
Full starboard roll.

00:30:21.514 --> 00:30:23.744
Evasive maneuvers,
lambda sequence.

00:30:24.751 --> 00:30:26.184
Fire.

00:31:01.254 --> 00:31:03.518
Shields at 85 percent
and holding.

00:31:03.556 --> 00:31:05.387
Minor damage reported, Deck 14.

00:31:05.425 --> 00:31:08.053
Come about to 143 mark 060.

00:31:08.094 --> 00:31:09.391
Coming about.

00:31:09.429 --> 00:31:10.453
Ready photons.

00:31:10.497 --> 00:31:12.795
Dispersal pattern sierra. Fire.

00:31:42.362 --> 00:31:44.830
I'm reading a massive discharge
on Deck 8.

00:31:44.864 --> 00:31:46.855
We've lost
a primary plasma conduit.

00:31:46.900 --> 00:31:48.959
Deck 8... Tierna's quarters.

00:31:49.002 --> 00:31:51.266
Damage control teams to Deck 8.

00:31:51.304 --> 00:31:53.397
I'm showing power failures
all over the ship.

00:32:01.447 --> 00:32:03.415
We've lost power
to the new holodeck grid.

00:32:03.449 --> 00:32:05.644
I can't restore it.

00:32:07.053 --> 00:32:08.042
B'Elanna, are you all right?

00:32:08.087 --> 00:32:09.281
Yes, Captain.

00:32:09.322 --> 00:32:12.086
But it looks like our reactant
injector controls were hit.

00:32:12.125 --> 00:32:13.092
Stand by.

00:32:13.126 --> 00:32:14.184
All three Kazon ships

00:32:14.227 --> 00:32:16.752
are concentrating
their fire on us now, Captain.

00:32:16.796 --> 00:32:18.696
Shields at 70 percent
and falling.

00:32:18.731 --> 00:32:20.858
Starboard targeting
scanners are off-line.

00:32:20.900 --> 00:32:23.368
Evasive maneuvers, Mr. Paris.
Gamma sequence.

00:32:23.403 --> 00:32:25.268
Engineering, I need warp power.

00:32:25.305 --> 00:32:26.966
We can't go to warp, Captain.

00:32:27.040 --> 00:32:29.531
The containment field
generator has been damaged.

00:32:29.576 --> 00:32:30.873
I'm attempting to bypass.

00:32:30.910 --> 00:32:33.401
Captain, if I can get a shuttle
through the crossfire,

00:32:33.446 --> 00:32:35.937
I can go back and bring
the Talaxians to help us.

00:32:37.917 --> 00:32:39.248
Chakotay, take the conn.

00:32:39.285 --> 00:32:40.582
Good luck, Lieutenant.

00:33:00.806 --> 00:33:02.068
Shuttle is clear.
So far, so good.

00:33:02.107 --> 00:33:04.405
Give him as much cover fire
as you can, Tuvok.

00:33:04.443 --> 00:33:05.637
Aye, Captain.

00:33:12.284 --> 00:33:13.751
Voyager to Paris.

00:33:16.255 --> 00:33:17.950
Please respond.

00:33:18.057 --> 00:33:19.422
Tom, can you hear me?

00:33:21.560 --> 00:33:23.152
I've lost contact
with the shuttle.

00:33:25.364 --> 00:33:27.161
Navigational array is off-line.

00:33:27.199 --> 00:33:29.258
We've lost power
to forward phasers.

00:33:30.436 --> 00:33:31.960
Shields at 30 percent.

00:33:32.004 --> 00:33:33.096
They're buckling.

00:33:36.875 --> 00:33:38.467
Report.

00:33:38.510 --> 00:33:40.410
The driver coil assembly
has been destroyed.

00:33:40.446 --> 00:33:42.311
Impulse engines are off-line.

00:33:42.347 --> 00:33:44.406
We're being boarded through
the shuttle bays, Captain.

00:33:44.450 --> 00:33:48.716
Phaser fights reported
on Decks 5, 6, 7.

00:33:48.754 --> 00:33:49.721
Intruder alert.

00:33:49.755 --> 00:33:51.484
Security to Decks 5 through 7.

00:33:51.523 --> 00:33:53.320
Begin evacuation.

00:33:53.358 --> 00:33:55.292
Janeway to computer.

00:33:55.327 --> 00:33:57.352
Initiate self-destruct sequence.

00:33:57.396 --> 00:34:00.160
Authorization: Janeway-pi-1-1-0.

00:34:00.199 --> 00:34:02.190
Set at ten minutes.

00:34:02.234 --> 00:34:04.725
Unable to initiate
self-destruct sequence

00:34:04.770 --> 00:34:07.500
due to damage
to secondary command processors.

00:34:10.275 --> 00:34:11.299
Stay where you are.

00:34:11.343 --> 00:34:12.332
Don't move!

00:34:16.882 --> 00:34:18.315
Hold your fire.

00:34:19.551 --> 00:34:20.540
Get down there!

00:34:21.687 --> 00:34:23.348
You! Move!

00:34:55.154 --> 00:34:56.746
I want to speak to Maje Culluh.

00:34:56.788 --> 00:34:58.983
Easily arranged, Captain.

00:35:01.260 --> 00:35:02.727
Hello, everyone.

00:35:04.129 --> 00:35:07.565
What do you think
of your son, Chakotay?

00:35:07.599 --> 00:35:08.930
He has your eyes.

00:35:08.967 --> 00:35:10.366
Don't you think?

00:35:10.402 --> 00:35:13.599
Thank goodness he doesn't look
too human.

00:35:13.639 --> 00:35:15.539
You all have
such weak foreheads.

00:35:15.574 --> 00:35:16.734
May he grow up never knowing

00:35:16.775 --> 00:35:18.572
the contempt his father has
for his mother.

00:35:18.610 --> 00:35:21.101
I think I can assure you
of that, Commander.

00:35:21.146 --> 00:35:23.410
I intend to take him
for my own son.

00:35:23.448 --> 00:35:26.940
A man who would violate a woman
under his own command...

00:35:26.985 --> 00:35:28.111
What?

00:35:28.153 --> 00:35:29.711
...doesn't deserve a son.

00:35:31.223 --> 00:35:32.383
Is that what she told you?

00:35:32.424 --> 00:35:35.325
The boy will be trained
as a Nistrim askara.

00:35:35.360 --> 00:35:38.488
Already he has helped us win the
greatest battle in our history.

00:35:38.530 --> 00:35:39.497
Culluh.

00:35:39.531 --> 00:35:42.125
I'd like to discuss
what happens now.

00:35:49.208 --> 00:35:53.668
You'll be given no more respect
than any Kazon woman...

00:35:53.712 --> 00:35:56.579
now that your ship
and technology are mine.

00:35:56.615 --> 00:35:59.743
I will tell you
when you may speak.

00:35:59.785 --> 00:36:00.979
Allow my crew to live.

00:36:01.086 --> 00:36:03.179
They were following my orders.

00:36:03.222 --> 00:36:04.746
You're even worse than she is.

00:36:05.824 --> 00:36:08.657
What is it about the women
from your Quadrant?

00:36:08.694 --> 00:36:12.528
You know she contradicts me
in front of the senior askara?

00:36:12.564 --> 00:36:17.024
My own woman disputing
her maje in front of others.

00:36:17.069 --> 00:36:19.128
This is your fault.

00:36:19.171 --> 00:36:21.696
You've let your women
get out of control.

00:36:21.740 --> 00:36:24.834
You know you have
my deepest respect, Maje.

00:36:26.979 --> 00:36:28.105
Why is it so dark in here?

00:36:28.146 --> 00:36:30.080
Somebody turn on the lights.

00:36:31.583 --> 00:36:34.780
Order the repair crews
to begin work immediately.

00:36:34.820 --> 00:36:38.881
I want to leave for the Hanon
system as soon as possible.

00:36:38.924 --> 00:36:40.482
What's in the Hanon system?

00:36:40.525 --> 00:36:42.254
Your new home.

00:36:42.294 --> 00:36:43.955
Take them to a cargo bay.

00:36:44.029 --> 00:36:45.963
Have the whole crew
brought there.

00:36:46.064 --> 00:36:47.156
Check all quarters.

00:36:51.336 --> 00:36:52.496
Move.

00:36:57.776 --> 00:36:59.334
Good-bye, Chakotay.

00:37:01.413 --> 00:37:03.472
I'll take good care of our son.

00:37:05.517 --> 00:37:09.214
Oh, are you hungry,
my brave little boy?

00:37:20.265 --> 00:37:22.426
You! Move!

00:37:22.467 --> 00:37:23.456
Keep moving!

00:37:27.839 --> 00:37:28.828
This is outrageous!

00:37:28.874 --> 00:37:30.501
Shut up!

00:37:41.386 --> 00:37:43.752
Computer, activate
medical holographic recall.

00:37:43.789 --> 00:37:44.949
Set for 12 hours.
Mark.

00:37:51.330 --> 00:37:52.228
Check every room.

00:37:53.298 --> 00:37:54.265
In here.

00:37:54.299 --> 00:37:55.664
Get back.

00:38:07.979 --> 00:38:08.968
Keep moving!

00:38:28.934 --> 00:38:31.300
Essential repairs
are complete, Maje.

00:38:31.336 --> 00:38:34.567
We have accounted for all but
two of the Federation crew.

00:38:34.606 --> 00:38:36.471
There is also a shuttle missing.

00:38:36.508 --> 00:38:38.874
Yes, we destroyed the shuttle
as it was leaving.

00:38:38.910 --> 00:38:40.537
Has that been confirmed?

00:38:43.515 --> 00:38:44.812
Fine.

00:38:44.850 --> 00:38:46.681
Have the other ships
send out search parties.

00:38:46.718 --> 00:38:48.948
Confirm the shuttle
was destroyed.

00:38:49.054 --> 00:38:50.146
And even if they find wreckage

00:38:50.188 --> 00:38:51.450
that seems to be
from the shuttle,

00:38:51.490 --> 00:38:53.720
tell them to check
for a recent warp trail.

00:39:07.739 --> 00:39:12.005
Stand by to engage
atmospheric thrusters.

00:39:17.549 --> 00:39:18.914
Prepare for landing.

00:39:18.950 --> 00:39:21.214
Activate the viewscreen.

00:39:26.258 --> 00:39:28.590
Extend landing struts.

00:39:38.403 --> 00:39:40.371
Ready environmental controls!

00:40:09.999 --> 00:40:11.762
Disengage engines.

00:40:13.670 --> 00:40:16.332
Secure thruster exhaust.

00:40:48.304 --> 00:40:50.670
A fitting end for a people

00:40:50.707 --> 00:40:53.335
who would not share
their technology.

00:40:53.376 --> 00:40:56.004
Let's see if you manage
to survive...

00:40:56.112 --> 00:40:58.273
without it.

00:41:04.721 --> 00:41:06.484
All right.

00:41:06.523 --> 00:41:07.547
Let's go.

00:41:07.590 --> 00:41:09.615
We've got to find
water and shelter.

00:41:26.109 --> 00:41:28.339
We'll divide
the crew into teams.

00:41:28.378 --> 00:41:30.312
Each of you will be
a team leader.

00:41:30.346 --> 00:41:33.281
Make it clear to all your people
that we expect to be rescued

00:41:33.316 --> 00:41:36.479
and our job is to survive
until help arrives.

00:41:36.519 --> 00:41:37.816
Do you really think it's likely

00:41:37.854 --> 00:41:39.344
that someone will find us,
Captain?

00:41:39.389 --> 00:41:40.583
You're the morale officer,
Neelix.

00:41:40.623 --> 00:41:41.988
You give me an answer.

00:41:42.025 --> 00:41:44.516
Help is on the way!

00:41:44.561 --> 00:41:47.291
Maybe Tom's shuttle got through.

00:41:47.330 --> 00:41:48.820
It's very important
that this crew

00:41:48.865 --> 00:41:49.991
be given a sense of hope.

00:41:50.033 --> 00:41:52.228
That's our most important
job right now.

00:41:52.268 --> 00:41:54.463
Our top priority
is drinking water.

00:41:54.504 --> 00:41:55.994
Second is shelter
to spend the night.

00:41:56.039 --> 00:41:57.631
A clearing
with a protected side

00:41:57.674 --> 00:41:59.938
like the base of a cliff
would be best.

00:41:59.976 --> 00:42:02.945
Food, fuel... look for all
the basic survival requirements.

00:42:03.012 --> 00:42:06.243
That includes anything that can
be used as a tool or a weapon.

00:42:06.282 --> 00:42:08.273
We'll reconvene here
in about two hours.

00:42:08.318 --> 00:42:10.047
All right,
start dividing the crew.

00:42:10.086 --> 00:42:12.554
Looks like we don't have
much daylight left.

00:42:12.589 --> 00:42:13.954
We'll spread the teams out

00:42:14.023 --> 00:42:15.854
in a standard
alpha search pattern

00:42:15.892 --> 00:42:17.189
to see what we have
to work with.

00:42:17.226 --> 00:42:18.955
Chakotay, Torres,
you're with me.

00:42:19.062 --> 00:42:20.359
Alpha team here.

00:42:20.396 --> 00:42:21.795
Beta team, this way.

00:42:21.831 --> 00:42:23.856
Gamma team.

00:42:23.900 --> 00:42:25.891
Delta team with me.

00:42:31.941 --> 00:42:34.409
The planet seems to be
seismically active.

00:42:34.444 --> 00:42:36.742
At first glance,
it's an M-Class planet

00:42:36.779 --> 00:42:38.974
in a Pliocene stage
of evolution.

00:42:39.082 --> 00:42:41.812
Comparable to Earth
several million years ago.

00:43:03.206 --> 00:43:04.400
Captain.
